  "live_records": {
    "q-264512": {
      "dom_id": "step-q264512",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X)).\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X))=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}).\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}_{22}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{{x}_{21}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} \\\\ \\frac{{x}_{12}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{-{x}_{11}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{4-1} & \\frac{1}{4-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4-1} & -\\frac{2}{4-1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
